## Why This Is Asked
This question tests SRE decision-making under pressure, understanding of error budget management, and the ability to balance business requirements with reliability commitments.

## Expected Answer
Strong candidates will: 1) Recognize that error budget exhaustion requires prioritizing reliability over new features, 2) Propose systematic performance optimization before introducing additional load, 3) Recommend a canary deployment strategy for controlled rollout, 4) Discuss comprehensive monitoring, alerting, and rollback procedures.

## Code Example
```typescript
// Error budget calculation and monitoring
const calculateErrorBudget = (slo: number, current: number) => {
  const errorBudget = (slo - current) / slo;
  return errorBudget > 0 ? errorBudget : 0;
};

// Feature rollout decision based on error budget
const canDeployFeature = (errorBudget: number, trafficIncrease: number) => {
  return errorBudget > (trafficIncrease * 0.1); // Conservative threshold
};
```

## Why This Is Asked

